  "featureGroup": false,
  "description": "The \u0027dss_connections_cached\u0027 dataset provides a comprehensive overview of cached connections within a Data Science Studio (DSS) environment. It includes detailed information about each connection, such as its name, type, and the mode of credential management. This dataset is particularly useful for administrators and data engineers who need to manage and audit connections to various data sources, such as PostgreSQL databases, EC2 instances, and filesystems. The dataset also includes parameters related to authentication, such as the type of authentication used and the scopes involved. Additionally, it provides metadata about who last modified the connection and whether writing is permitted. This information is crucial for ensuring secure and efficient data access and management within a DSS platform. The dataset can be used to automate connection audits, monitor access permissions, and streamline the management of data source connections.",
  "shortDesc": "Dataset of cached DSS connections with details on type, credentials, and access.",
